# Several gems in one `path` source, each gemspec named otherwise
# (`billing_engine.gemspec` for billing-engine): the gemspec was looked up
# by file name only, so both gems fell back to `components/`, and which one
# owned its files was HashMap order — the other was a `clear` row, flipping
# between runs. Bundler takes the gemspec whose `name` is the gem's, and so
# does trekr. Two gems found in one directory (a_kit, b_kit) are told apart
# from neither: both rows, lowered, rather than one picked.
dead Gemfile billing-engine=none shipping-engine=none a_kit=unreferenced~told b_kit=unreferenced~told
